    "transcript": {
        "duration": 41,
        "text": "Over 70% of Uber's pull requests are now written by AI agents. Uber's engineers double their code output in one year. Uber just shared numbers on its AI-driven engineering setup, and they're wild. More than 70% of pull requests across its few thousand engineers are now generated by local or cloud agents. The lines of code per engineer doubled year over year. The company ran over 250 automated migrations, rewriting 9 million lines of code without engineers touching them. Everything routes through one internal model gateway, over 100 million model requests per day, with PE reduction and safety checks running in under 100 milliseconds. If you want the breakdown, just comment Uber and I'll send it to you.",
